PATCH 487: FUN_0000_af1c, the COLLISION-AVOIDANCE scan, was fully base-lost (host-deref'd cursor and
candidates, `int *` scaling that advanced the display table 8 bytes per 4-byte entry and read [si+0x2c]
where the asm reads [si+0x16]).

asm 0xaf1c-0xaf96 (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00), di = the moving object's NEAR offset (aea8 passes it raw): the walk
state lives in DGROUP -- word[0x97a2] is the 0xdfbc display-table cursor (stride 4) and word[0x97a4] the
remaining count (182).  A candidate must be non-null, not type 0x15, carry byte[si+0x16]&0x40 and not be
the mover; b112's bearing must put it in the forward half-plane (bearing - word[di+0x10] < 0x4000 or
>= 0xc000) and its Manhattan distance |dX|+|dY| must be <= 0x1e00.  Then word[0x97a0]=0x400 and a930 (the
swept proximity test, patch 475) decides: CF=1 (impending collision) returns, CF=0 keeps walking; an
exhausted walk returns CF=0.  INDIA1's self-play SEGV'd here once patch 486 let its units reach the scan.
b112 and a930 take HOST pointers (patches 334/475), so the near offsets are rebased at those calls.
